    - link "Usage" [ref=e144]
  - text: "app/layout.tsx"
  - generic [ref=e145] [scrollable]:
    - button "Copy" [ref=e146]
    - text: "import { SidebarProvider, SidebarTrigger } from \"@/components/ui/sidebar\"\nimport { AppSidebar } from \"@/components/app-sidebar\"\n \nexport  default  function  Layout({ children }: { children: React.ReactNode }) {\n  return (\n    <SidebarProvider>\n      <AppSidebar />\n      <main>\n        <SidebarTrigger />\n        {children}\n      </main>\n    </SidebarProvider>\n  )\n}"
  - text: "components/app-sidebar.tsx"
  - generic [ref=e147]:
    - button "Copy" [ref=e148]
    - text: "import {\n  Sidebar,\n  SidebarContent,\n  SidebarFooter,\n  SidebarGroup,\n  SidebarHeader,\n} from \"@/components/ui/sidebar\"\n \nexport  function  AppSidebar() {\n  return (\n    <Sidebar>\n      <SidebarHeader />\n      <SidebarContent>\n        <SidebarGroup />\n        <SidebarGroup />\n      </SidebarContent>\n      <SidebarFooter />\n    </Sidebar>\n  )\n}"
  - heading [level=2]:
    - link "Composition" [ref=e149]
  - text: "Use the following composition to build a  Sidebar  layout:"
  - generic [ref=e150]:
    - button "Copy" [ref=e151]
    - text: "SidebarProvider\n├── Sidebar\n│   ├── SidebarHeader\n│   ├── SidebarContent\n│   │   ├── SidebarGroup\n│   │   │   ├── SidebarGroupLabel\n│   │   │   ├── SidebarGroupAction\n│   │   │   ├── SidebarGroupContent\n│   │   │   └── SidebarMenu\n│   │   │       ├── SidebarMenuItem\n│   │   │       │   ├── SidebarMenuButton\n│   │   │       │   ├── SidebarMenuAction\n│   │   │       │   └── SidebarMenuBadge\n│   │   │       └── SidebarMenuItem\n│   │   │           ├── SidebarMenuButton\n│   │   │           └── SidebarMenuSub\n│   │   │               ├── SidebarMenuSubItem\n│   │   │               └── SidebarMenuSubItem\n│   │   └── SidebarGroup\n│   │       └── SidebarMenu\n│   │           ├── SidebarMenuItem\n│   │           └── SidebarMenuItem\n│   ├── SidebarFooter\n│   └── SidebarRail\n├── SidebarInset\n└── SidebarTrigger"
  - heading [level=2]:
    - link "Structure" [ref=e152]
  - text: "SidebarProvider — Handles collapsible state and provides sidebar context to child components.\nSidebar — The main collapsible sidebar panel.\nSidebarHeader — Sticky at the top; use for branding, titles, or workspace switchers.\nSidebarFooter — Sticky at the bottom; use for user menus, settings, or actions.\nSidebarContent — Scrollable region between the header and footer.\nSidebarGroup — Groups related navigation with optional label, action, and content areas.\nSidebarMenu / SidebarMenuItem — Menu structure for links, badges, actions, and nested submenus.\nSidebarRail — Resize handle for adjusting sidebar width when applicable.\nSidebarInset — Wraps main content when using the  inset  variant.\nSidebarTrigger — Control that toggles the sidebar open or collapsed.\n\nSidebar Structure"
  - heading [level=2]:
    - link "SidebarProvider" [ref=e153]
  - text: "The  SidebarProvider  component is used to provide the sidebar context to the  Sidebar  component. You should always wrap your application in a  SidebarProvider  component."
  - heading [level=3]:
    - link "Props" [ref=e154]
  - text: "Name Type Description defaultOpen boolean Default open state of the sidebar.open boolean Open state of the sidebar (controlled).onOpenChange(open: boolean) => void Sets open state of the sidebar (controlled)."
  - heading [level=3]:
    - link "Width" [ref=e155]
  - text: "If you have a single sidebar in your application, you can use the  SIDEBAR_WIDTH  and  SIDEBAR_WIDTH_MOBILE  variables in  sidebar.tsx  to set the width of the sidebar.\ncomponents/ui/sidebar.tsx"
  - generic [ref=e156]:
    - button "Copy" [ref=e157]
    - text: "const  SIDEBAR_WIDTH = \"16rem\"\nconst  SIDEBAR_WIDTH_MOBILE = \"18rem\""
  - text: "For multiple sidebars in your application, you can use the --sidebar-width  and --sidebar-width-mobile  CSS variables in the  style  prop."
  - generic [ref=e158]:
    - button "Copy" [ref=e159]
    - text: "<SidebarProvider\n   style={\n    {\n      \"--sidebar-width\": \"20rem\",\n      \"--sidebar-width-mobile\": \"20rem\",\n    } as  React.CSSProperties\n  }\n>\n  <Sidebar />\n</SidebarProvider>"
  - heading [level=3]:
    - link "Keyboard Shortcut" [ref=e160]
  - text: "To trigger the sidebar, you use the  cmd+b  keyboard shortcut on Mac and  ctrl+b  on Windows.\ncomponents/ui/sidebar.tsx"
  - generic [ref=e161]:
    - button "Copy" [ref=e162]
    - text: "const  SIDEBAR_KEYBOARD_SHORTCUT = \"b\""
  - heading [level=2]:
    - link "Sidebar" [ref=e163]
  - text: "The main  Sidebar  component used to render a collapsible sidebar."
  - heading [level=3]:
    - link "Props" [ref=e164]
  - text: "Property Type Description side left  or  right The side of the sidebar.variant sidebar, floating, or  inset The variant of the sidebar.collapsible offcanvas, icon, or  none Collapsible state of the sidebar.\nProp Description offcanvas A collapsible sidebar that slides in from the left or right.icon A sidebar that collapses to icons.none A non-collapsible sidebar."
  - alert: "Note: If you use the  inset  variant, remember to wrap your main content\nin a  SidebarInset  component."
  - generic [ref=e165]:
    - button "Copy" [ref=e166]
    - text: "<SidebarProvider>\n  <Sidebar  variant=\"inset\" />\n  <SidebarInset>\n    <main>{children}</main>\n  </SidebarInset>\n</SidebarProvider>"
  - heading [level=2]:
    - link "useSidebar" [ref=e167]
  - text: "The  useSidebar  hook is used to control the sidebar."
  - generic [ref=e168]:
    - button "Copy" [ref=e169]
    - text: "import { useSidebar } from \"@/components/ui/sidebar\"\n \nexport  function  AppSidebar() {\n  const {\n    state,\n    open,\n    setOpen,\n    openMobile,\n    setOpenMobile,\n    isMobile,\n    toggleSidebar,\n  } = useSidebar()\n}"
  - text: "Property Type Description state expanded  or  collapsed The current state of the sidebar.open boolean Whether the sidebar is open.setOpen(open: boolean) => void Sets the open state of the sidebar.openMobile boolean Whether the sidebar is open on mobile.setOpenMobile(open: boolean) => void Sets the open state of the sidebar on mobile.isMobile boolean Whether the sidebar is on mobile.toggleSidebar() => void Toggles the sidebar. Desktop and mobile."
  - heading [level=2]:
    - link "SidebarHeader" [ref=e170]
  - text: "Use the  SidebarHeader  component to add a sticky header to the sidebar.\ncomponents/app-sidebar.tsx"
  - generic [ref=e171]:
    - button "Copy" [ref=e172]
    - text: "<Sidebar>\n  <SidebarHeader>\n    <SidebarMenu>\n      <SidebarMenuItem>\n        <DropdownMenu>\n          <DropdownMenuTrigger  render={<SidebarMenuButton />}>\n            Select Workspace\n            <ChevronDown  className=\"ml-auto\" />\n          </DropdownMenuTrigger>\n          <DropdownMenuContent>\n            <DropdownMenuItem>\n              <span>Acme Inc</span>\n            </DropdownMenuItem>\n          </DropdownMenuContent>\n        </DropdownMenu>\n      </SidebarMenuItem>\n    </SidebarMenu>\n  </SidebarHeader>\n</Sidebar>"
  - heading [level=2]:
    - link "SidebarFooter" [ref=e173]
  - text: "Use the  SidebarFooter  component to add a sticky footer to the sidebar."
  - generic [ref=e174]:
    - button "Copy" [ref=e175]
    - text: "<Sidebar>\n  <SidebarFooter>\n    <SidebarMenu>\n      <SidebarMenuItem>\n        <SidebarMenuButton>\n          <User2 /> Username\n        </SidebarMenuButton>\n      </SidebarMenuItem>\n    </SidebarMenu>\n  </SidebarFooter>\n</Sidebar>"
  - heading [level=2]:
    - link "SidebarContent" [ref=e176]
  - text: "The  SidebarContent  component is used to wrap the content of the sidebar. This is where you add your  SidebarGroup  components. It is scrollable."
  - generic [ref=e177]:
    - button "Copy" [ref=e178]
    - text: "<Sidebar>\n  <SidebarContent>\n    <SidebarGroup />\n    <SidebarGroup />\n  </SidebarContent>\n</Sidebar>"
  - heading [level=2]:
    - link "SidebarGroup" [ref=e179]
  - text: "Use the  SidebarGroup  component to create a section within the sidebar.\nA  SidebarGroup  has a  SidebarGroupLabel, a  SidebarGroupContent  and an optional  SidebarGroupAction."
  - generic [ref=e180]:
    - button "Copy" [ref=e181]
    - text: "<SidebarGroup>\n  <SidebarGroupLabel>Application</SidebarGroupLabel>\n  <SidebarGroupAction>\n    <Plus /> <span  className=\"sr-only\">Add Project</span>\n  </SidebarGroupAction>\n  <SidebarGroupContent></SidebarGroupContent>\n</SidebarGroup>"
  - text: "To make a  SidebarGroup  collapsible, wrap it in a  Collapsible."
  - generic [ref=e182] [scrollable]:
    - button "Copy" [ref=e183]
    - text: "<Collapsible  defaultOpen  className=\"group/collapsible\">\n  <SidebarGroup>\n    <SidebarGroupLabel  render={<CollapsibleTrigger />}>\n      Help\n      <ChevronDown  className=\"ml-auto transition-transform group-data-open/collapsible:rotate-180\" />\n    </SidebarGroupLabel>\n    <CollapsibleContent>\n      <SidebarGroupContent />\n    </CollapsibleContent>\n  </SidebarGroup>\n</Collapsible>"
  - heading [level=2]:
    - link "SidebarMenu" [ref=e184]
  - text: "The  SidebarMenu  component is used for building a menu within a  SidebarGroup.\nSidebar Menu"
  - generic [ref=e185]:
    - button "Copy" [ref=e186]
    - text: "<SidebarMenu>\n  {projects.map((project) => (\n    <SidebarMenuItem  key={project.name}>\n      <SidebarMenuButton  render={<a  href={project.url} />}>\n        <project.icon />\n        <span>{project.name}</span>\n      </SidebarMenuButton>\n    </SidebarMenuItem>\n  ))}\n</SidebarMenu>"
  - heading [level=2]:
    - link "SidebarMenuButton" [ref=e187]
  - text: "The  SidebarMenuButton  component is used to render a menu button within a  SidebarMenuItem.\nBy default, the  SidebarMenuButton  renders a button but you can use the  render  prop to render a different component such as a  Link  or an  a  tag.\nUse the  isActive  prop to mark a menu item as active."
  - generic [ref=e188]:
    - button "Copy" [ref=e189]
    - text: "<SidebarMenuButton  render={<a  href=\"#\" />} isActive>\n  Home\n</SidebarMenuButton>"
  - heading [level=2]:
    - link "SidebarMenuAction" [ref=e190]
  - text: "The  SidebarMenuAction  component is used to render a menu action within a  SidebarMenuItem."
  - generic [ref=e191]:
    - button "Copy" [ref=e192]
    - text: "<SidebarMenuItem>\n  <SidebarMenuButton  render={<a  href=\"#\" />}>\n    <Home />\n    <span>Home</span>\n  </SidebarMenuButton>\n  <SidebarMenuAction>\n    <Plus /> <span  className=\"sr-only\">Add Project</span>\n  </SidebarMenuAction>\n</SidebarMenuItem>"
  - heading [level=2]:
    - link "SidebarMenuSub" [ref=e193]
  - text: "The  SidebarMenuSub  component is used to render a submenu within a  SidebarMenu."
  - generic [ref=e194]:
    - button "Copy" [ref=e195]
    - text: "<SidebarMenuItem>\n  <SidebarMenuButton />\n  <SidebarMenuSub>\n    <SidebarMenuSubItem>\n      <SidebarMenuSubButton />\n    </SidebarMenuSubItem>\n  </SidebarMenuSub>\n</SidebarMenuItem>"
  - heading [level=2]:
    - link "SidebarMenuBadge" [ref=e196]
  - text: "The  SidebarMenuBadge  component is used to render a badge within a  SidebarMenuItem."
  - generic [ref=e197]:
    - button "Copy" [ref=e198]
    - text: "<SidebarMenuItem>\n  <SidebarMenuButton />\n  <SidebarMenuBadge>24</SidebarMenuBadge>\n</SidebarMenuItem>"
  - heading [level=2]:
    - link "SidebarMenuSkeleton" [ref=e199]
  - text: "The  SidebarMenuSkeleton  component is used to render a skeleton for a  SidebarMenu."
  - generic [ref=e200]:
    - button "Copy" [ref=e201]
    - text: "<SidebarMenu>\n  {Array.from({ length: 5 }).map((_, index) => (\n    <SidebarMenuItem  key={index}>\n      <SidebarMenuSkeleton />\n    </SidebarMenuItem>\n  ))}\n</SidebarMenu>"
  - heading [level=2]:
    - link "SidebarTrigger" [ref=e202]
  - text: "Use the  SidebarTrigger  component to render a button that toggles the sidebar."
  - generic [ref=e203]:
    - button "Copy" [ref=e204]
    - text: "import { useSidebar } from \"@/components/ui/sidebar\"\n \nexport  function  CustomTrigger() {\n  const { toggleSidebar } = useSidebar()\n \n  return <button  onClick={toggleSidebar}>Toggle Sidebar</button>\n}"
  - heading [level=2]:
    - link "SidebarRail" [ref=e205]
  - text: "The  SidebarRail  component is used to render a rail within a  Sidebar. This rail can be used to toggle the sidebar."
  - generic [ref=e206]:
    - button "Copy" [ref=e207]
    - text: "<Sidebar>\n  <SidebarHeader />\n  <SidebarContent>\n    <SidebarGroup />\n  </SidebarContent>\n  <SidebarFooter />\n  <SidebarRail />\n</Sidebar>"
  - heading [level=2]:
    - link "Controlled Sidebar" [ref=e208]
  - text: "Use the  open  and  onOpenChange  props to control the sidebar."
  - generic [ref=e209]:
    - button "Copy" [ref=e210]
    - text: "export  function  AppSidebar() {\n  const [open, setOpen] = React.useState(false)\n \n  return (\n    <SidebarProvider  open={open} onOpenChange={setOpen}>\n      <Sidebar />\n    </SidebarProvider>\n  )\n}"
  - heading [level=2]:
    - link "Theming" [ref=e211]
  - text: "We use the following CSS variables to theme the sidebar."
  - generic [ref=e212]:
    - button "Copy" [ref=e213]
    - text: "@layer  base {\n  :root {\n    --sidebar-background: 0  0% 98%;\n    --sidebar-foreground: 240  5.3% 26.1%;\n    --sidebar-primary: 240  5.9% 10%;\n    --sidebar-primary-foreground: 0  0% 98%;\n    --sidebar-accent: 240  4.8% 95.9%;\n    --sidebar-accent-foreground: 240  5.9% 10%;\n    --sidebar-border: 220  13% 91%;\n    --sidebar-ring: 217.2  91.2% 59.8%;\n  }\n \n  .dark {\n    --sidebar-background: 240  5.9% 10%;\n    --sidebar-foreground: 240  4.8% 95.9%;\n    --sidebar-primary: 0  0% 98%;\n    --sidebar-primary-foreground: 240  5.9% 10%;\n    --sidebar-accent: 240  3.7% 15.9%;\n    --sidebar-accent-foreground: 240  4.8% 95.9%;\n    --sidebar-border: 240  3.7% 15.9%;\n    --sidebar-ring: 217.2  91.2% 59.8%;\n  }\n}"
  - heading [level=2]:
    - link "Styling" [ref=e214]
  - text: "Here are some tips for styling the sidebar based on different states."
  - generic [ref=e215]:
    - button "Copy" [ref=e216]
    - text: "<Sidebar  collapsible=\"icon\">\n  <SidebarContent>\n    <SidebarGroup  className=\"group-data-[collapsible=icon]:hidden\" />\n  </SidebarContent>\n</Sidebar>"
  - generic [ref=e217] [scrollable]:
